    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm working on a fintech app redesign and need to make sure we're hitting wcag 2.1 standards. can u give me a quick checklist for color contrast and screen reader stuff?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For color contrast, ensure all text and important interface elements meet WCAG AA standards, which generally requires a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 against its background. Regarding screen readers, always provide descriptive, meaningful `alt` text for all images and use proper semantic HTML tags so assistive technologies can correctly interpret your page structure. Additionally, make sure all interactive elements are keyboard-focusable and operable without a mouse.",
      "source": "target",
