    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thx. can u expand a bit on the screen reader stuff? specifically for things like dynamic content updates or when a user triggers a popup/modal. i want to make sure nothing gets lost when the UI changes unexpectedly.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For dynamic updates, use ARIA live regions (like `aria-live=\"polite\"`) so screen readers announce content changes when they happen, such as error messages or successful form submissions. When opening a modal or popup, you must trap the focus within that element and use `aria-modal=\"true\"` to inform assistive technologies that the content behind it is inert. Finally, always programmatically manage focus—ensure focus moves logically into the new modal or dynamically added content area.",
      "source": "target",
