    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. i'm also worried about those weird little edge cases where the accessibility features might fail or where something just breaks in a way that's hard to track. what are some common pitfalls or 'ghost' bugs that usually pop up with screen readers?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A common pitfall is inconsistent labeling, where an element visually has a label but technically lacks one for the accessibility tree. Another frequent issue is managing focus traps incorrectly, causing users to lose their place when navigating complex components. Also, custom controls built without proper ARIA roles can be invisible to screen readers entirely. Thoroughly test on multiple screen readers and browsers to uncover these subtle, yet critical, inconsistencies.",
      "source": "target",
